# The importer fixture CSVs are BYTE-EXACT test vectors: the CRLF row
# endings, the LF-only embedded newline inside a quoted cell, and the UTF-8
# characters ARE what the suites assert against. Line-ending normalization
# (core.autocrlf) would rewrite exactly the bytes under test — so these
# files opt out of text handling entirely, on every platform.
scripts/fixtures/*.csv -text
